  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The isomers of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, that can be prepared by&nbsp;Gabriel phthalimide synthesis are primary amines.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d3766ddd-accd-4f25-990a-ab33fae728ad.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 115px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>can be prepared by Gabriel phthalimide synthesis because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> is possible in</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3be53aab-14d5-4929-9624-6ea28eda5c9e.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>Secondary&nbsp;amines react&nbsp;with Hinsberg&rsquo;s reagent to give solid insoluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math>. Hence, Q is the secondary amine</p><p><img height=\"160\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fad2d793-3b7c-4602-a8f3-f3156fe0d22e.png\" width=\"213\" /></p><p>Aromatic amines like aniline give diazonium salts. The&nbsp;diazonium&nbsp;salt used in diazo coupling to get red dye with beta Naphthol in sodium hydroxide. Hence, R is aromatic amine as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9df1c553-58f0-46ac-97fc-5e432854851e.png\" style=\"width: 275px; height: 161px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
